cards.en:
Before learning CSS, the book shows the simplest way to style an element: write the declarations directly in the element's <b>style attribute</b>. This is called an <b>inline style</b>.<pre>&lt;p style="color:blue; text-align:center"&gt;
  Lily thinks it's wonderful to fly.
&lt;/p&gt;</pre>Rules:<ul><li>The value of the <b>style</b> attribute is a list of <b>property: value</b> pairs.</li><li>Pairs are separated by <b>semicolons ;</b>.</li><li>The style affects <b>only this one element</b> (and the text inside it).</li></ul>Inline style uses almost the same syntax as a CSS declaration block, just without the selector and curly brackets. Inline styles also have the <b>highest specificity</b> (see 1.3), so they always win over a stylesheet for the same property.

cards.zh:
最简单的样式写法：把声明直接写进元素的 <b>style attribute</b>，叫 <b>inline style</b>。<pre>&lt;p style="color:blue; text-align:center"&gt;
  Lily thinks it's wonderful to fly.
&lt;/p&gt;</pre>规则：<ul><li>style 属性的值是一串 <b>property: value</b>。</li><li>多个之间用<b>分号 ;</b> 分隔。</li><li>只影响<b>这一个元素</b>。</li></ul>语法和 CSS 的 declaration block 几乎一样，只是没有 selector 和花括号。Inline style 的 <b>specificity 最高</b>（见 1.3），同一 property 一定压过样式表。

cards.en:
A CSS rule has two parts:<pre>h1 {
  background-color: coral;
  text-decoration: underline;
}</pre><ul><li>The <b>selector</b> (<code>h1</code>) states <b>which elements</b> the rule applies to.</li><li>The <b>declaration block</b> (everything inside <b>{ }</b>) contains one or more <b>declarations</b>.</li></ul>A <b>declaration</b> assigns <b>one value to one style property</b>, e.g. <code>color: #6A567F;</code><br>Rules to memorise:<ul><li>The whole block is wrapped in <b>curly brackets { }</b>.</li><li>Each declaration has a <b>property</b> and a <b>value</b>, separated by a <b>colon :</b></li><li>Declarations are separated by <b>semicolons ;</b></li></ul>The syntax inside the block is almost the same as an inline style. A common exam error is writing <code>=</code> instead of <code>:</code>, or missing the closing bracket.

cards.zh:
一条 CSS 规则有两部分：<pre>h1 {
  background-color: coral;
  text-decoration: underline;
}</pre><ul><li><b>Selector</b>（h1）：指定规则作用于<b>哪些元素</b>。</li><li><b>Declaration block</b>（<b>{ }</b> 里）：包含一条或多条 <b>declaration</b>。</li></ul><b>Declaration</b> = 给<b>一个 style property 赋一个 value</b>，如 <code>color: #6A567F;</code><br>要背的规则：<ul><li>整个块用<b>花括号 { }</b> 包住</li><li>property 和 value 用<b>冒号 :</b> 分开</li><li>declarations 之间用<b>分号 ;</b></li></ul>块内语法与 inline style 几乎相同。常见错误：用 = 代替 :，或漏写右括号。

ex.a:
Errors: round brackets instead of curly brackets; <code>=</code> instead of <code>:</code>; comma instead of semicolon.<pre>p {
  color: blue;
  font-size: 14px;
}</pre>

cards.en:
The <b>element-wise selector</b> (type selector) is the simplest selector. It must be a <b>valid HTML element name</b> written <b>without any symbol</b> in front: <code>p</code>, <code>ul</code>, <code>li</code>, <code>table</code>, <code>img</code>, <code>tr</code>...<br><br>Its declaration block is applied to <b>all elements of that type in the document</b>.<pre>&lt;style&gt;
  p {
    color: purple;
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
&lt;/style&gt;</pre>Every &lt;p&gt; on the page becomes purple and underlined, but &lt;h1&gt; or &lt;li&gt; text is not affected.<br><br>Use it for a site-wide look (e.g. all paragraphs use Arial). Because it is the <b>least specific</b> selector, a class, ID or inline style can override it for special elements.

Almost every HTML element can have an optional <b>id attribute</b>. It is a <b>unique identifier</b>: <b>each id must be unique within one web page</b> (HTML document). Two elements on the same page must not share an id.<br><br>An <b>ID selector</b> is <b>#</b> followed by the id. Its declarations apply <b>only to the element with that id</b>.<pre>&lt;style&gt;
  #name {
    background-color: coral;
    color: white;
    text-align: center;
  }
&lt;/style&gt;
&lt;h1 id="name"&gt;Lily's Bio&lt;/h1&gt;</pre>You can write several ID selectors to style several individual elements. Note: the <b>#</b> appears only in the CSS, not in the HTML attribute (<code>id="name"</code>, not <code>id="#name"</code>). ID selectors have <b>higher specificity than class and element selectors</b>.

cards.zh:
几乎所有 HTML 元素都可加可选的 <b>id attribute</b>，是 <b>unique identifier</b>：<b>同一网页内每个 id 必须唯一</b>。<br><br><b>ID selector</b> = <b>#</b> + id，声明<b>只作用于该 id 的元素</b>。<pre>&lt;style&gt;
  #name {
    background-color: coral;
    color: white;
    text-align: center;
  }
&lt;/style&gt;
&lt;h1 id="name"&gt;Lily's Bio&lt;/h1&gt;</pre>可写多个 ID selector 分别设置多个元素。注意：<b>#</b> 只写在 CSS，HTML 里是 <code>id="name"</code>，不是 <code>id="#name"</code>。ID selector 的 specificity <b>高于 class 和 element</b>。

cards.en:
A <b>class selector</b> is a <b>. (dot)</b> followed by a class name. Its declarations apply to <b>any element whose class attribute contains that name</b>, whatever the element type.<pre>.girl   { color: pink; }
.senior { text-decoration: underline; }</pre>Add the class in HTML with the <b>class attribute</b>. One element can have <b>several classes separated by spaces</b>:<pre>&lt;li class="senior"&gt;James He (F5, Boy)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class="girl senior"&gt;Sandy Huang (F5, Girl)&lt;/li&gt;</pre>Sandy gets both styles: pink and underlined.<br><br>Naming rule: a class name <b>cannot contain spaces</b> (a space means 'two classes'). Join words with a <b>hyphen</b> (<code>sci-teacher</code>) or <b>underscore</b> (<code>sci_teacher</code>). Classes are ideal for groups (all girls, all seniors, all sale items).

From highest to lowest priority:<br><b>Inline styles &gt; ID selector (#intro, #name) &gt; Class selector (.strong, .highlight) &gt; Element-wise selector (p, h1, tr)</b><br><br>The more precisely a selector points at one element, the higher its specificity: an ID names one element, a class names a group, an element selector names every element of a type.<pre>#intro { color: red; }
.highlight { color: blue; }
&lt;h1 id="intro" class="highlight"&gt;...&lt;/h1&gt;</pre>→ <b>red</b>: ID beats class, <b>no matter which rule is written first</b>. The 'later wins' rule is only for selectors of <b>equal</b> specificity.<br><br>Method for exam tracing: for each property, list every rule that matches the element, then pick the highest specificity; if tied, the later one.

cards.zh:
由高到低：<br><b>Inline styles &gt; ID selector (#intro, #name) &gt; Class selector (.strong, .highlight) &gt; Element-wise selector (p, h1, tr)</b><br><br>Selector 指得越精确，specificity 越高：ID 指一个元素，class 指一组，element selector 指所有同类元素。<pre>#intro { color: red; }
.highlight { color: blue; }
&lt;h1 id="intro" class="highlight"&gt;...&lt;/h1&gt;</pre>→ <b>红色</b>：ID 胜 class，<b>与书写先后无关</b>。“后者胜”只用于<b>同级</b>。<br><br>考试追踪方法：每个 property 列出所有匹配规则，取 specificity 最高的；同级取后者。

cards.en:
When two selectors with the <b>same specificity</b> (e.g. two class selectors) match the same element and set the same property, the declaration <b>defined later in the document</b> is applied.<pre>.intro { color: green; }
.highlight { color: red; }

&lt;p class="intro highlight"&gt;...&lt;/p&gt;</pre>Result: <b>red</b>, because .highlight is defined after .intro.<br><br>'Later' means the position of the rule in the CSS (the stylesheet order), <b>not</b> the order of class names inside the class attribute (see the misconception card). If both rules set different properties, both apply; only the conflicting property is decided by order.

cards.zh:
两个<b>同 specificity</b> 的 selector（如两个 class）选中同一元素并设同一 property 时，<b>文档中较后定义</b>的声明被应用。<pre>.intro { color: green; }
.highlight { color: red; }

&lt;p class="intro highlight"&gt;...&lt;/p&gt;</pre>结果：<b>红色</b>，因为 .highlight 定义在后。<br><br>“后”指规则在 CSS 中的位置，<b>不是</b> class 属性里 class 名的顺序（见误区卡）。不冲突的 property 两者都生效，只有冲突的那条按次序决定。

cards.en:
Changing an element's tag can change which rules match it.<pre>#title { color: red; }
p { color: blue; font-size: 10px; }
&lt;p id="title"&gt;University of Hong Kong (HKU)&lt;/p&gt;</pre>As a &lt;p&gt;: text is <b>red</b> (ID beats p) and <b>10px</b> (from p, no conflict).<br><br>If changed to <code>&lt;h1 id="title"&gt;</code>: the <b>p element selector no longer matches</b>, so it loses font-size 10px. The h1 <b>default style</b> applies: larger and bold. The <b>colour stays red</b>, because #title still matches.<br><br><b>Book error:</b> Checkpoint 1.3's code opens with &lt;p id="title"&gt; but closes with &lt;/h1&gt; (line 21) and writes <code>colour</code>; correct HTML needs matching tags and CSS needs <code>color</code>.

cards.zh:
更换元素标签会改变匹配到的规则。<pre>#title { color: red; }
p { color: blue; font-size: 10px; }
&lt;p id="title"&gt;University of Hong Kong (HKU)&lt;/p&gt;</pre>作为 &lt;p&gt;：<b>红色</b>（ID 胜 p）、<b>10px</b>（来自 p，无冲突）。<br><br>改成 <code>&lt;h1 id="title"&gt;</code>：<b>p 选择器不再匹配</b>，失去 10px，改用 h1 <b>默认样式</b>：更大、粗体。<b>颜色仍是红色</b>，因为 #title 仍匹配。<br><br><b>课本错误：</b>Checkpoint 1.3 开标签 &lt;p id="title"&gt; 却用 &lt;/h1&gt; 结束（第 21 行），且写 colour；正确 HTML 要标签配对、CSS 要用 color。

cards.en:
An <b>internal style sheet</b> puts the CSS inside the HTML file, between <b>&lt;style&gt;</b> and <b>&lt;/style&gt;</b>. In theory the &lt;style&gt; element can go anywhere, but the <b>best practice is to put it in &lt;head&gt;</b>: this improves readability and keeps CSS from getting entangled with the HTML in &lt;body&gt;.<pre>&lt;head&gt;
  &lt;style&gt;
    .girl { color: pink; }
  &lt;/style&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;</pre><b>Advantages:</b> CSS and HTML are in <b>one file</b>, convenient for small projects or few styles; <b>faster loading</b>, since the browser does not need to request a separate .css file.<br><b>Disadvantages:</b> <b>limited reusability</b>: the CSS cannot be used by other HTML files; with many pages, each has its own internal style sheet, so the site is <b>hard to maintain</b>.<br>Modern practice: most CSS in external files; internal only for page-specific styles.

