cards.en:
JavaScript code must be placed between <b>&lt;script&gt;</b> and <b>&lt;/script&gt;</b>. The script element can be put <b>anywhere</b> in the HTML document, in &lt;head&gt; or in &lt;body&gt;.<pre>&lt;head&gt;
  &lt;script&gt;
    let name = "Linda";
  &lt;/script&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;</pre>The browser renders the HTML and executes the JavaScript <b>sequentially</b> (top to bottom), so the position matters: code that runs immediately cannot use an element that has not been created yet.<br><br>Modern web pages usually put JavaScript in the <b>&lt;head&gt;</b> to <b>separate the layout (HTML body) from the functionality (JavaScript)</b>. The interactive parts are written as <b>functions</b>, which only run when a condition is met or an event occurs, so the position no longer causes problems.

