cards.en:
Use the <b>+ operator</b> on strings to join them into one string (<b>concatenation</b>).<pre>let a = "Hello";
let b = "World";
console.log(a + " " + b);   // Hello World</pre>When a String and a Number are joined with +, the <b>number is first converted to a string</b>: <code>"Score: " + 5</code> gives "Score: 5", and <code>"5" + 3</code> gives <b>"53"</b>, not 8. Expressions are evaluated left to right: <code>1 + 2 + "3"</code> is "33" but <code>"1" + 2 + 3</code> is "123".<br><br>Language comparison: Python and JavaScript use <b>+</b>; <b>PHP uses the dot (.)</b>. Remember to add spaces yourself; + does not insert any.

