while (n &lt;= 50) {
  n = n * 3;
}</pre>

cards.en:
A <b>for loop</b> iterates through a range of numbers. Syntax:<pre>for (let i = 0; i &lt; 5; i++) {
  console.log(i);   // 0 1 2 3 4
}</pre>The three parts in the brackets, separated by <b>semicolons</b>:<ol><li><b>initialisation</b> (let i = 0) runs once;</li><li><b>condition</b> (i &lt; 5) checked before each iteration;</li><li><b>update</b> (i++) runs after each iteration.</li></ol>Unlike Python's range(), you write the condition yourself. Counting down: <code>for (let i = 10; i &gt; 0; i--)</code>; step 2: <code>i += 2</code>. To loop through an array use <code>i &lt; arr.length</code> (indices 0 to length - 1).

